From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 02:10:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 43/93] soc: apple: mcc: wait for display controllers to retire
 boot scanout

A display controller can keep scanning out the framebuffer the
bootloader left on screen after it binds, and also while its node stays
disabled because the bootloader kept the boot framebuffer as the
display. For a boot DMA supplier that an enabled simple-framebuffer
names as its display, enable cache allocation only once the display
driver reports that a displayed swap of its own has retired that
scanout. Other suppliers still only need to be bound. A supplier
phandle that does not resolve, or a detached consumer or supplier
node, leaves allocation off.

The display driver reserves the record before it can retire the
scanout, so the one-shot retirement cannot be lost to an allocation
failure. Retirement survives either driver's unbind and reprobe;
records and waiters are dropped when a node they name is detached, and
none is added or retried for a detached node.

OF flags a node detached before it calls the reconfig notifiers, so
probe cannot hold a detach off, but the notifier always runs after the
flag is set. Probe therefore checks its nodes and enables allocation
under the lock the detach notifier takes, and registers the enabled
controller there. Either probe sees the flag and fails, or the notifier
finds the controller and turns allocation off, unless the detached node
is a supplier whose boot scanout already retired, and cancels the
enable a wake from deep sleep would do. Suspend, resume and shutdown
take the same lock. A failed enable's write-back (up to 100 ms per
plane) is done under that lock and delays a detach by as much. A
deferred controller is retried outside the display driver's receive
path.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
